// where the value is not null, instead of saying it may be null and advising a check of the same value.
// @expect-error Cannot read a member of 'string?' because 'text' is null here. This branch runs only when 'text == null'. Read it in an 'else' branch, or after the 'if' once this branch has returned, where 'text' is not null.
// @expect-error Cannot call a member of 'Item?' because 'item' is null here. This branch runs only when 'item != null' is false. Call it in the 'if' branch, where 'item' is not null.
// A loop that writes the value reads it again on the next pass, when the test no longer proves it null, so the read says it may be null.
// @expect-error Cannot index 'int[]?' because it may be null here. Check 'rows' for null first ('if (rows != null)').
// A loop that leaves the value alone keeps the read in the branch that proves it null.
